220
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:30,550
Uh, okay.

221
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,842
Nice chatting with you, I guess.

222
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:36,234
Do you know people in this town, Pedro?

223
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,700
We can talk later.

224
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,510
Uh-huh!

225
00:12:42,593 --> 00:12:45,240
So your name's Pudding, huh? Well, thanks.

226
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:47,060
You saved our butts. Oh, no.

227
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,242
Don't say that.

228
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:51,820
I'm the one who should be
thanking all of you. Yeah, why?

229
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,691
Because of what you said.

230
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:56,420
that it was too delicious.

231
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:02,077
The chocolate at the cafe is the
new blend I just came up with.

232
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:04,748
Tell me, did it melt
in your mouth properly?

233
