242
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,280
She's too sweet.

243
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:34,040
You really like making chocolate, huh?

244
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:37,020
I gotta tell you, I'm
wild about sweet stuff.

245
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:40,777
In fact, just smelling chocolate
everywhere is enough to make me happy.

246
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:43,300
Eating's good, too. That's lovely.

247
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:46,797
I don't mean to be rude, especially
since you've been so generous?

248
00:13:46,880 --> 00:13:49,640
but we really need to get going. I see.

249
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:51,940
That's a shame. Well?

250
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,417
How about you have a cup of tea first?

251
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,853
Something to follow up all those sweets.

252
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:58,966
Oh, why, that sounds perfect.

253
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:01,298
All right, this shouldn't take long.

254
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,200
Oh, my god.

255
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:05,340
She is such a sweet girl.

256
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,080
I'm sorry, I forgot to ask your name.

257
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,060
I'm Monkity Luffy.

258
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:13,877
I'm going to be a king of the world.

259
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:14,790
Seriously?

260
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:15,790
Huh?

261
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:22,740
Luffy?

262
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:59,737
How a songer will it be till
we have our tea for tea?

263
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,820
Only three days, Mama.

264
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:04,820
How long is that sound?

265
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:07,980
Tell me what is to be done with Jermason.

266
00:15:08,420 --> 00:15:10,900
Soon we'll have him, Mama.

267
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:14,320
Couches, sofas, dressers, teapots.

268
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:20,637
All will be shall be,

269
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:25,380
all will be shall be,
all kings are lovely,

270
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:29,420
all kings are lovely, that design, divine,

271
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:31,157
and the prize, only mercy,

272
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,740
our remediants, take them,

273
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:36,797
but will flow if they resist,

274
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:43,457
mercy

275
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:44,370
ends!

276
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:47,500
They're mine.

277
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,280
Nice to go!

278
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:52,920
It's mine.

279
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:54,842
And the fruits!

280
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,220
It is mine.

281
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,740
Time to make a cake so good!

282
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:05,077
The finest cake you'll ever eat.

283
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:07,460
such sweet insanity.

284
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,477
Tea time. And hell?

285
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:12,160
what a party.

286
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:17,260
Is this some strawberry jam?

287
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:20,600
Either way, I don't give a damn!

288
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:24,122
And if you don't show your
sleep, they'll be low!

289
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,820
Social and bleeding is sacrificial!

290
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:32,260
Oh, it's a dreamland
with joy never ending!

291
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:35,620
Everyone is welcome,
our harmony is blending!

292
00:16:37,660 --> 00:16:38,760
To the land!

293
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:54,617
Hmm i heard that he's here is he

294
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:58,100
truly near yes he is oh it's true

295
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:04,640
Your mind strong hat

296
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,020
Your name is Luffy?

297
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,080
That was a mistake!

298
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:24,280
Now that I look closer,
I do recognize you!

299
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:26,000
You're Straw Hat Luffy!

300
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,180
That's right!

301
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:31,536
And I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

302
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,340
We're all dead men walking now.

303
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:37,840
Wait a minute.

304
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:41,177
You people aren't really the
Straw Hat Pirates, are you?

305
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:42,580
Yep, that's us.

306
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:44,968
Sanji's crewmates are here?

307
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,600
It can't be true.

308
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,480
I just told you it is.

309
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,326
Are you even listening to me?

310
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,620
Wait, do you know Sanji?

311
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,600
What? What?

312
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:08,977
You're seriously the lady
who's supposed to marry Sanji?

313
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:10,900
Big mom is your mom?

314
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:15,560
It is her. No way.

315
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:16,960
Sanji's so lucky.

316
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:19,220
What a beautiful bride to be.

317
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:22,702
You said bride.

318
00:18:24,820 --> 00:18:26,217
I don't understand.

319
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:27,157
And...

320
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,340
you aren't even Mama's allies.

321
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,233
How did you get through Tart's security?

322
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:35,197
If she finds out you're here, you'll...

323
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,680
you'll all be killed.

324
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:40,277
You shouldn't have come to her territory.

325
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:43,120
She's a very scary pirate. Huh?

326
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:44,510
Huh?

327
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:48,760
And here's the Straw Hats, so
you're all scary pirates, too!

328
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:51,480
Help me!

329
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,217
Relax, you're okay.

330
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,840
We won't attack you.

331
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:01,760
Hey, Luffy, want me to kill her?

332
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:03,100
What did I say?

333
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,300
Back off!

334
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,140
So, that's what you want.

335
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:13,220
You plan to take him away.

336
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:18,320
I knew it, Mama is forcing him.

337
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:20,780
This is the way she does business.

338
00:19:21,220 --> 00:19:23,573
In order to strengthen her pirate group,

339
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:26,366
she often arranges
marriages for her children.

340
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,580
There's no hope.

341
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:31,547
All of us have given up
on marrying for love.

342
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:34,880
You can either accept it or run away.

343
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:39,114
One of my older sisters did the latter.

344
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:43,080
She ran off to sea a while
back in search of a husband.

345
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:45,580
Of her choosing.

346
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:51,677
I hope you'll pardon my curiosity,

347
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:56,080
but the invitation says you're the
35th daughter of the Charlottes?

348
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:58,137
There can't be that many, right?

349
00:19:58,220 --> 00:19:59,200
That'd be silly.

350
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:01,170
No.

351
00:20:01,253 --> 00:20:04,480
There are 39 of us
girls, and 46 boys, too.

352
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:07,426
So Mama's actually got
85 children altogether.

353
00:20:07,780 --> 00:20:09,760
That's a lot of kids! That many?

354
00:20:10,220 --> 00:20:13,220
Hopefully your dad helps
out around the house, too!

355
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:19,640
Mama has 43 husbands, so if you count her
plus us and our fathers, it's 129 people.

356
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:20,870
Huh?

357
00:20:20,953 --> 00:20:22,289
How is that even possible?

358
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:27,117
Some of my older brothers and sisters
already have children of their own, too.

359
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:30,024
So if you include them,
the total's even higher.

360
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:31,917
Do you want to know something else?

361
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,235
Almost all the Big Mom pirates
are our blood relatives.

362
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,860
Talk about a Big Mom.

363
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:48,872
So anyway, Pudding, have you
and Sanji met each other yet?

364
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:51,370
I...

365
00:20:51,453 --> 00:20:52,980
yeah, but just once.

366
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:59,500
His eyebrows are rather strange,
but he's a very kind and gentle man.

367
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:00,980
Flower, flower!

368
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,877
Sometimes his eyes turn into hearts,

369
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:05,977
but he taught me so
much about making sweets

370
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,937
that I don't really mind things like that.

371
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:09,160
Flower, flower!

372
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,820
We like the same things,
and he's so manly!

373
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:16,397
And I hear his legs are black,
but it's all the same to me.

374
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:18,020
He is cool, huh?

375
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:23,680
You know that's not why
they call him Black Lake.

376
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:25,580
Yep, that's our Sanji.

377
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:28,512
There's lots of awesome things about him.

378
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:32,740
Wait, I recognize that expression.

379
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:34,680
You love him, don't you?

380
00:21:36,060 --> 00:21:37,760
You're in love with Sanji?

381
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:39,100
Be honest with us.

382
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:40,630
Oh, why?

383
00:21:40,713 --> 00:21:41,960
I shouldn't say.

384
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:46,940
But then, uh, Mama's
decision can't be overturned.

385
00:21:47,860 --> 00:21:51,880
If I chose my husband,
then, well, he would be.

386
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:54,777
Oh, that's great.

387
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:56,060
I like Sanchi, too.

388
00:21:57,040 --> 00:21:58,080
We're twinsies.

389
00:21:58,360 --> 00:22:00,242
Oh, no, I can't say it out loud.

390
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:06,220
So Sanchi's engaged to
a darling young lady?

391
00:22:06,520 --> 00:22:09,991
And for once it isn't someone
who rejects all his advances?

392
00:22:10,260 --> 00:22:12,789
If I had eyes, they'd
be heart-shaped, too.

393
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:18,140
I'm sorry, but I think
we'd better tie her up.

394
00:22:26,820 --> 00:22:28,977
She's clearly going to
tell them where we are

395
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:31,766
and if they find us here
on the outer islands?

396
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:35,100
And there's no way we'll
make it to where Sanji is.

397
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:38,100
You can't treat her like that. Stop it.

398
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:40,241
We have to keep her quiet somehow

399
00:22:40,900 --> 00:22:44,700
Don't forget that girl
is a daughter of big mom.

400
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:49,020
Yeah, I know But she's
obviously afraid of her too.

401
00:22:49,580 --> 00:22:51,357
Which is why she'll tell her!

402
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:53,322
But we can't know that for sure!

403
00:22:53,660 --> 00:22:54,836
You gotta pipe down!

404
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,560
Excuse me

405
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:11,880
If I try, I can abandon
my feelings for Sanji.

406
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:13,940
I can let him go.

407
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:24,360
The people of Toto Land.

408
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:29,960
They gave us their blessing.

409
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:36,437
Celebrating the same goes
for the Vinsmoke family

410
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:39,217
and Mama's really looking
forward to the wedding!

411
00:23:39,300 --> 00:23:45,197
Cake no one can disobey
an order from her so

412
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:48,257
I knew I couldn't marry
for love despite that.

413
00:23:48,340 --> 00:23:52,737
I've dreamed about it since I was little I

414
00:23:52,820 --> 00:23:56,220
wondered about my soulmate
what he'd be like? You know?

415
00:23:57,220 --> 00:24:00,300
Then one day, I got to meet my Sanji.

416
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:16,950
Huh?

417
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:22,620
I was surprised the groom
was someone so wonderful.

418
00:24:24,320 --> 00:24:27,967
But right before the end of our
meeting, he told me something.

419
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:34,920
I really would like to marry
you, but I'm afraid I just can't.

420
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:41,004
Because I want to go back
to be with my friends.

421
00:24:41,660 --> 00:24:42,490
What?

422
00:24:43,280 --> 00:24:45,120
Sanchi rejected a girl?

423
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:48,300
Oh, wow.

424
00:24:48,660 --> 00:24:53,200
If he said no to you, then
he must really love our crew.

425
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:57,240
And that feeling is obviously mutual.

426
00:24:57,980 --> 00:24:59,627
Because you're all here now.

427
00:24:59,820 --> 00:25:04,055
I mean, you are risking your lives
by traveling to Toto Land to get him.

428
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:11,020
No matter what Mama says, I can't marry
Sanji if that isn't what he wants.

429
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:12,300
That'd be awful.

430
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:14,580
But more than that,

431
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:18,532
It's clear to me now how
important he is to his crewmates.

432
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:22,220
So I can't take him away.

433
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:28,588
After all, the heart wants what
the heart wants, as they say.

434
00:25:28,840 --> 00:25:32,546
Which is why, if this is what
Sanji's heart wants, then I'm in.

435
00:25:33,760 --> 00:25:35,348
You should take this route.

436
00:25:37,340 --> 00:25:40,300
It's the one path you can
use to avoid Mama's eye.

437
00:25:40,660 --> 00:25:42,542
Only her children know about it.

438
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:44,740
And that leads to Sanji?

439
00:25:45,120 --> 00:25:49,440
If you follow this map, eventually
you should reach Whole Cake Island.

440
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:53,624
But Mama won't let him
slip through her fingers.

441
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:58,440
I say we rendezvous tomorrow
at the coast right here, okay?

442
00:26:00,820 --> 00:26:04,560
I promise I'll bring Sanji
there whatever the cost.

443
00:26:04,900 --> 00:26:06,380
Let's all work together.

444
00:26:06,840 --> 00:26:07,820
You don't mind?

445
00:26:08,180 --> 00:26:10,137
Don't you think Big Mom will punish you?

446
00:26:10,220 --> 00:26:13,460
Mama and I are family,
so don't worry about me.

447
00:26:14,280 --> 00:26:15,560
It's worse for you.

448
00:26:15,860 --> 00:26:17,520
You're in hostile territory.

449
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:19,270
Puddin.

450
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:28,460
My dear, this must be painful for you.

451
00:26:28,620 --> 00:26:30,677
You and Sanji care about each other.

452
00:26:30,760 --> 00:26:32,172
This is the right thing.

453
00:26:34,180 --> 00:26:35,380
Warms my heart.

454
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:37,220
That is if I had one.

455
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:39,346
This is heartbreaking for me.

456
00:26:39,620 --> 00:26:42,444
But I'll just try and
focus on my future suitor.

457
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:45,137
Maybe he'll be even more incredible.

458
00:26:45,220 --> 00:26:48,397
Oh, you're such a gracious young lady.

459
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:52,100
It's hard to believe you're
the child of someone so scared.

460
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:57,057
This is great, thanks!

461
00:26:57,140 --> 00:26:58,820
I'm happy to help out.

462
00:27:03,860 --> 00:27:06,997
Lady Pudding, your
escort is ready for you.

463
00:27:07,080 --> 00:27:08,360
One moment.

464
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:10,897
I'm in the middle of something.

465
00:27:10,980 --> 00:27:12,200
I'll be right out.

466
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:18,416
Forgive me, my lady, but you must
stop working until after the wedding.

467
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:19,560
Stop working?

468
00:27:19,660 --> 00:27:20,940
But I have customers.

469
00:27:21,380 --> 00:27:23,145
You need to make preparations.

470
00:27:31,580 --> 00:27:33,120
Oh, hey, it's you.

471
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:35,457
I've got the groceries you ordered.

472
00:27:35,540 --> 00:27:37,364
You're welcome to pick them up.

473
00:27:38,100 --> 00:27:39,037
Food, finally!

474
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:39,950
You got all that?

475
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:42,160
We'll be okay. Thanks a lot.

476
00:27:45,260 --> 00:27:46,800
Chocolate burgers, too?

477
00:27:47,180 --> 00:27:49,800
We have enough, Luffy. Now let's go.

478
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:51,037
Peckham's is waiting.

479
00:27:51,120 --> 00:27:52,920
But I want one really bad.

480
00:27:55,740 --> 00:27:56,860
Chocolate pasta.

481
00:27:57,140 --> 00:27:58,552
Chocolate fried chicken.

482
00:27:58,820 --> 00:28:00,237
Stop looking at other stuff.

483
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,200
We have to go.

484
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:09,200
Anyone see him?

485
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:10,697
I don't think so.

486
00:28:10,780 --> 00:28:12,074
Well, this is unusual.

487
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:13,560
Is he pooping?

488
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:15,720
Check the toilet. Hey!

489
00:28:18,220 --> 00:28:20,220
There's a message in the bathroom!

490
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:21,190
Huh?

491
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:29,440
Turn back!

492
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:31,060
What the heck?

493
00:28:31,220 --> 00:28:32,497
Did Peckhams write that?

494
00:28:32,580 --> 00:28:33,960
No one else was aboard.

495
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:35,280
Were we attacked?

496
00:28:35,740 --> 00:28:37,020
Where'd Peckhams go?

497
00:28:37,180 --> 00:28:38,597
You think he got abducted?

498
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:45,260
Just speculating but maybe we've been
found out regardless this is quite serious.

499
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:52,524
So they're trying to tell us that if we
don't turn back something bad will happen!

500
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:56,800
All right everyone keep
that in mind i guess.

501
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:05,040
Okay let's go.

502
00:29:06,740 --> 00:29:09,060
This is starting to get real good.

503
00:29:52,360 --> 00:29:53,760
Fire!

504
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:04,420
All done here? Yes, sir.

505
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:05,830
Good.

506
00:30:05,913 --> 00:30:06,743
Let's go.

507
00:30:08,320 --> 00:30:10,540
You killed my wife.

508
00:30:11,540 --> 00:30:12,893
You killed my children.

509
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:16,080
You left my country in ruins.

510
00:30:16,980 --> 00:30:18,600
You germ of bastards.

511
00:30:18,960 --> 00:30:21,725
I'll send you to hell
where you belong, dammit!

512
00:30:22,380 --> 00:30:23,210
Wall.

513
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:46,277
I can't believe this took four hours.

514
00:30:46,360 --> 00:30:48,577
My brother's wedding is soon.

515
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:50,300
I'm in a hurry.

516
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:57,155
I don't give a damn about your family.

517
00:30:58,500 --> 00:30:59,657
Or your war.

518
00:30:59,740 --> 00:31:01,160
They're both irrelevant.

519
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:09,717
Well, we're done.

520
00:31:09,800 --> 00:31:12,157
I can't believe these pathetic countries.

521
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:14,181
Kept this up for two whole years?

522
00:31:15,740 --> 00:31:16,858
Got the commission?

523
00:31:17,060 --> 00:31:18,260
You bet I did.

524
00:31:37,100 --> 00:31:39,017
They saved our country.

525
00:31:39,100 --> 00:31:41,197
The world may call them demons?

526
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:42,357
But they're wrong.

527
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:44,637
To us. Well.

528
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:46,600
These are angels.

529
00:31:48,380 --> 00:31:50,200
Put down your weapons, men.

530
00:31:50,460 --> 00:31:52,900
At long last, the war is over.

531
00:31:56,760 --> 00:31:58,840
We love you, Jarba!

532
00:31:59,300 --> 00:32:02,320
Jarba, number six, thank you.

533
00:32:03,640 --> 00:32:07,120
Jarba, Jarba, Jarba, Jarba.

534
00:32:13,160 --> 00:32:15,337
The wedding's in three days.

535
00:32:15,420 --> 00:32:18,714
We can make it to Whole Cake
Island in two days, easily.

536
00:32:19,040 --> 00:32:20,340
What about Sanji?

537
00:32:21,520 --> 00:32:23,100
He's already here.

538
00:32:23,840 --> 00:32:25,240
Really? Perfect.

539
00:32:25,660 --> 00:32:27,240
I can't wait to see him.

540
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:29,120
Is that a joke?

541
00:32:29,580 --> 00:32:31,080
We'll be there soon.

542
00:32:31,940 --> 00:32:32,770
Kali!
